<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luitpoldings</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Luitpoldings were a Bavarian noble dynasty that ruled the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in the late ninth and tenth centuries. Its founder, Margrave Luitpold, fell fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyars</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Pressburg</a> in 907, and his son Arnulf made Bavaria a powerful stem duchy within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a>. After 947 the Ottonian kings gave the duchy to their own relatives, though a Luitpolding held it again briefly in the 980s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luitpoldings.jpg" alt="Luitpoldings" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hohenfeld · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luitpolding.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
